Copying takes linear time because every medicine name must be copied. 10. Alternative Concept and Complexity Analysis If std::vectorstd::string is used instead of a dynamically allocated array, the compiler-generated copy constructor automatically performs an independent deep copy.

Example: #include #include using namespace std;

class Prescription { vector medicines;

public: Prescription(int n) : medicines(n) {} };

Method Time Complexity Space Complexity Shallow copy O(1) O(1) additional Deep copy using array O(n) O(n) Deep copy using vector O(n) O(n)

The vector approach follows the Rule of Zero because memory management is handled automatically. 11. Conclusion Thus, deep copying was successfully implemented using a copy constructor, copy assignment operator and destructor. The copied prescription objects maintain independent memory, preventing unwanted modifications and double deletion.
